#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train, merges directly. A workflow PR needs no approval beyond the batch card (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Workflow PRs, A)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Add the merge-train label instead of merging; the train lands the batch with one CI run."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:68
#. Diagram label
msgid "All green per rule 1?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:124
#. Diagram label
msgid "Awaiting the owner"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:121
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Do not merge. The next wake reads the checks again."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:125
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Do not merge. The owner's tap on the card wakes the next pass."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Enforce the pacing rule of continual-progress (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Cancel CI): close superseded or duplicate PRs, such as a re-pin whose commits another open PR already carries, and cancel their runs; cancel stale queued runs that never started, never a main push run that has started; ask the owners of P3 PRs to return them to draft."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every 10 minutes in the merge window, and hourly outside it, as a backstop. Otherwise a subscribed PR event, a main run finishing, or a sibling's message wakes it. Never a polling loop inside a turn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every check run on the head SHA has finished, and anything pending blocks; wait for every tier, e2e included. The full tier ran (the No new failures judge, or every full test shard); a draft or fast-tier-only pass never counts. Every judge passes (owner ruling, 2026-11-07): an aggregate job covers only the parts it names, and each test shard's own no-new-failures table lists 0 new failures; with no judge, each check concluded success, skipped or neutral. A cancelled job counts only when a later run of the same workflow on the same head passed that job. merge:watch prints this verdict per PR."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:100
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge it through merge:guard"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:13
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge manager watch: wake, read the queue live, route"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:18
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:95
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge train"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:138
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:120
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not green yet"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:133
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nothing"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:117
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nothing to do"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Offer the card and land only on the owner's tap."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One card per batch, naming each PR, in priority order: P0 main-red fixes and the re-pin chain, P1 work they unblock, P2 CI speed, P3 the rest."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owner approved?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Put it on the owner's batch card"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:44
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read live, never from a stored copy: the open PRs (draft, head, mergeable, owed checks, open owner decisions), the queued and running runs with the age of the oldest, the latest main push run, and each PR owner's last push or comment."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:43
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read PRs, runner queue, main verdict and owners"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:131
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Relieve the runners"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:88
#. Diagram label
msgid "Rides the train?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:130
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturated"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:50
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Saturated: queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or the owner says the runners are full. Stalled: a PR owner has been silent for 2+ hours. Ready: a PR stacks with green owed CI. Otherwise nothing."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturation meta-merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:132
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell the owner, then take the stalled PR over."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The loop run by the agent that holds the merge-steward lane (actor merge-manager, skill merge-manager-watcher), which coordinates with the swarm siblings whenever a batch lands. Each wake reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and the PR owners live, and routes to one sub-process. A wake with nothing to do ends with no message. Every merge on any route waits for the owner's own OK, given in the merge manager's session as one card per batch (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge manager, holding the merge-steward role across one or more repositories. Each wake it reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and who owns each PR, then routes to the process the queue needs (merge train, saturation meta-merge, stalled-agent takeover) or stays idle."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "Timer, PR event, main run done, or sibling message"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "Wake handled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:49
#. Diagram label
msgid "What does the queue need?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:137
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes for a folio-assistant PR that does not change .github/workflows/. No for a workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Train, A)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the owner tapped this batch's card in the merge manager's session, or said to merge this PR when green. An approval given in a sibling's session does not count (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B)."
msgstr ""
